  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nWV imagery indicates a northwest flow aloft prevailing across\nthe Western High Plains downstream of a ridge centered across \nthe Desert Southwest. Near the surface, a lee side trough of low\npressure is slowly strengthening across eastern Colorado.\n\nMinimal thunderstorm chances (20%) exist across west central/central \nKansas this evening as the SREF indicates a weak upper level \nshortwave and associated H5 vort maxima cycling southeast off \nthe ridge axis in the Northern Rockies into the high plains of \nwestern Nebraska and northeast Colorado. Near the surface, \nprevailing southerlies will support pooling moisture ahead of an\nadvancing dryline, providing modest instability with MUCAPE \nvalues upward of 1000 J/kg or so. Despite weaker dynamic support\naloft, steeping mid- level lapse rates in vicinity of an axis \nof increased low level convergence associated with the dryline \nwill set the stage for potential isolated thunderstorm \ndevelopment this evening as H5 vort maxima transition through. \nThis is suggested by a few CAMs and the HREF pointing to only a \n10 to 20% probability of 6-hr QPF exceeding a mere 0.1 of an \ninch in vicinity of the I-70 corridor by late evening. \nHotter/drier conditions are likely the next couple of days as \nsouthwesterly downsloping enhances a drier air mass across the \nWestern High Plains.\n\nVery warm temperatures are forecast tonight as southwesterly \ndownsloping reinforces a warmer air mass across southwest/central \nKansas. With the HREF painting a 70-90% probability of temperatures \ndropping below 75F in west central and extreme southwest Kansas to \nto only a 10-20% probability of slipping below 75F in south central \nKansas, look for lows generally down into 70s(F). Southwesterly \ndownsloping will further enhance drier air into southwest Kansas \nSunday, nudging H85 temperatures up from Saturday with a little \nabove 30C in central Kansas to near 35C near the Colorado line. \nExpect widespread afternoon highs topping 100F with the HREF showing \na widespread 80-90% probability of temperatures exceeding the \ncentury mark. Similar conditions are likely Monday.",
